This work addresses the challenge of optimizing large language models for reasoning tasks by enhancing their efficiency and performance through difficulty-aware training and fine-grained token advantage estimation. Both DIET and KTAE aim to improve reasoning capabilities by dynamically adjusting model behavior based on task difficulty and token-specific contributions, respectively. Experimental results demonstrate significant improvements in inference scaling and response quality while reducing token counts.
